[direction] d-04 -> blocked (The numerical X-ray limits exist only in figures. Digitising them (get_paper_figures plus reading the curves) and adding 2207.04572 to references.bib did not fit in the tool budget, and NuSTAR does not cover 45 keV.)
**Blocked — Obtain quote-verified X-ray upper limits on sin^2 2theta versus m_s for keV sterile neutrinos over roughly 5-50 keV. Use them to define 'X-ray-allowed mixing' for d-01 and to test whether 100% DW dark matter is excluded independently of Lyman-alpha..** (The numerical X-ray limits exist only in figures. Digitising them (get_paper_figures plus reading the curves) and adding 2207.04572 to references.bib did not fit in the tool budget, and NuSTAR does not cover 45 keV.) Half the success criteria are met: the literature statements on whether pure Dodelson-Widrow (DW) production can be all of the dark matter are quote-verified, but the numerical table of X-ray limits on sin^2 2theta could not be built. (1) Literature statements, all quote-verified. Merle 2017 (arXiv:1702.08430) says DW production is 'nowadays known to be excluded by observations'; that rests on structure formation together with X-ray bounds (f-007). Roach et al. 2022 (arXiv:2207.04572, NuSTAR Milky Way halo, about 7 and 20 Ms per detector) set sin^2 2theta limits for m_s = 6-40 keV. They 'strongly disfavor a ~7-keV sterile neutrino' (the 3.5 keV line candidate) and give leading limits at about 15-18 and 25-40 keV, 'reaching or extending below the big bang nucleosynthesis limit'. They also state that the parameter space is 'mostly covered' (this includes satellite-counting bounds), but that this 'does not fully rule out sterile neutrinos as the only DM component'; only the simple mixing production mechanism 'may be insufficient' (f-008). So no source makes a clean claim that X-ray limits alone exclude 100% DW dark matter. Roach et al. 2020 (arXiv:1908.09037) give 95% limits on the decay rate Gamma (not on sin^2 2theta) for 10-40 keV, plotted in their Fig. 5 on an axis of 1e-29 to 1e-27 s^-1. They are about 2x better at 10-12 keV and weaker near 16 keV and 30-40 keV (f-009). Perez et al. 2017 (arXiv:1609.00667) give the strongest limits over most of 10-50 keV (f-004). (2) Not established: numerical sin^2 2theta limits at 7, 20, 22, 29 and 45 keV, so the X-ray-allowed f_s,max for d-01 cannot be computed yet. The papers give the limits only as figure curves, which were not digitised (dead end x-02). NuSTAR coverage ends at 40 keV, so 45 keV needs INTEGRAL/SPI or Fermi-GBM limits. (3) Files: the 2207.04572 full text is at /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-research-lyman-wdm/runs/261019_110120/2207.04572.txt. 2207.04572 has not yet been added to references.bib; the earlier sources 1609.00667, 1908.09037 and 1702.08430 are already cited there. Next step: run get_paper_figures on 2207.04572 (its final sin^2 2theta-versus-m_s figure) or 1908.09037 (Fig. 1, the combined plot), read the limits as approximate values, and add 2207.04572 to references.bib.
