[finding] f-014 The sterile-nu server's DW yield gives a smaller f_s=1 mixing than both published fits I read: sin^2 2theta(f_s=1) is 2.55e-10, 3.95e-11, 3.32e-11, 2.02e-11 and
**Finding:** The sterile-nu server's DW yield gives a smaller f_s=1 mixing than both published fits I read: sin^2 2theta(f_s=1) is 2.55e-10, 3.95e-11, 3.32e-11, 2.02e-11 and 9.17e-12 at 7.1, 20, 22, 29 and 45 keV (from the CSV rows at sin^2 2theta = 1e-12: Omega_s h^2 = 0.000471462, 0.00304114, 0.00361029, 0.00593606, 0.0130907). The Abazajian 2006 fit gives 3.02e-10 x10 = 3.02e-9, 5.61e-10, 4.80e-10, 3.06e-10 and 1.50e-10, which is 11.9, 14.2, 14.4, 15.2 and 16.4 times the tool's values. The Asaka-Laine-Shaposhnikov 'most conservative' upper-bound line gives 7.88e-10, 1.30e-10, 1.10e-10, 6.79e-11 and 3.16e-11, which is 3.10, 3.29, 3.31, 3.36 and 3.44 times the tool's values. So the tool produces 3 to 16 times more DW dark matter per unit mixing than these fits.
