[tool] d-05 post_finding {"claim": "At the 3.5 keV line point (7.1 keV, sin^2 2theta = 7e-11), the DW fraction depends on the normalisation: f_s = 0.275 with the tool, 7e-11/7.88e-10 = 
[finding] f-015 At the 3.5 keV line point (7.1 keV, sin^2 2theta = 7e-11), the DW fraction depends on the normalisation: f_s = 0.275 with the tool, 7e-11/7.88e-10 = 0.089 with 
**Finding:** At the 3.5 keV line point (7.1 keV, sin^2 2theta = 7e-11), the DW fraction depends on the normalisation: f_s = 0.275 with the tool, 7e-11/7.88e-10 = 0.089 with the ALS conservative line, and 7e-11/3.02e-9 = 0.023 with Abazajian 2006. The headline DW production fraction is therefore uncertain by a factor of about 3 to 12. The tool is the most optimistic of the three (largest f_s), so its X-ray exclusion of f_s = 1 at 20 keV (f-002) only gets stronger under the published normalisations.
[tool] tc-261019_1-w2-d-05-102 -> ok: Recorded finding f-015.
[tool] d-05 post_finding {"claim": "Combined table of allowed DW fraction versus mass (Lyman-alpha side). At 7.1 keV: 0812.0010 gives F_wdm < 0.35 (quote-verified, d-02), and 2504.06367
[finding] f-016 Combined table of allowed DW fraction versus mass (Lyman-alpha side). At 7.1 keV: 0812.0010 gives F_wdm < 0.35 (quote-verified, d-02), and 2504.06367 mapped to 
**Finding (preliminary):** Combined table of allowed DW fraction versus mass (Lyman-alpha side). At 7.1 keV: 0812.0010 gives F_wdm < 0.35 (quote-verified, d-02), and 2504.06367 mapped to DW mass gives f between 0.16 and 0.35 (my estimate; the mapped points are 4.4 and 11 keV). It is also below the 0812.0010 pure-DW floor of 12.1 keV, so the binding constraint is Lyman-alpha mixed-DM, f_s <~ 0.2-0.35. At 20 and 22 keV: 2504.06367 mapped gives f <~ 0.5-0.67 (mapped points 18 and 28 keV), and 20/22 keV are below the 29 keV (4.1 keV variant) and 45 keV (5.7 keV variant) Viel-mapped pure-DW floors. The tool's X-ray check excludes f_s = 1 at 20 keV, so the binding constraint is Lyman-alpha (f <~ 0.5-0.67) unless a numerical X-ray limit is stricter. At 29 keV: f = 1 is allowed by Lyman-alpha only for the 4.1 keV variant (floor ~29 keV, unverified Viel mapping), while for the 5.7 keV variant f <~ 0.67 or more. At 45 keV: f = 1 is allowed by Lyman-alpha even for the 5.7 keV variant (floor ~45 keV). At 29 and 45 keV, X-ray limits are presumably binding, but no numerical X-ray limit is available, so f_s,max(X-ray) stays undetermined.
[tool] tc-261019_1-w2-d-05-103 -> ok: Recorded finding f-016.
